{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778977092737,"sessionID":"ses_1ccb71acfffePYPEX97Uqgm6bA","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"apply_patch","callID":"call_EiWBSBg4Mk1LVKsnoc4nE5yy","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"patchText":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: /__w/eval-ont-agent-mondo/eval-ont-agent-mondo/ISSUE_COMMENTS.md\n+Implemented locally and committed; changes can be referenced in PR #<NN>.\n+\n+Added new term `MONDO:7770012` `preneoplastic lesion` as a child of `MONDO:0021074` `precancerous condition`, following the issue discussion that it should not be modeled as a subtype of `pre-malignant neoplasm`.\n*** Add File: /__w/eval-ont-agent-mondo/eval-ont-agent-mondo/PR_COMMENTS.md\n+Added a new MONDO term for `preneoplastic lesion` and committed it locally.\n+\n+Changes made:\n+- Created `MONDO:7770012` `preneoplastic lesion`\n+- Added parent: `MONDO:0021074` `precancerous condition`\n+- Added a text definition based on the issue request, framed to distinguish the concept from `pre-malignant neoplasm` by describing a precancerous clonal lesion state rather than an established neoplasm\n+- Linked the term back to issue `#9781`\n+\n+Rationale:\n+- The issue discussion clarified that `preneoplastic lesion` should be a new term, not an exact synonym of `precancerous condition`\n+- The requester also clarified that it should not be placed under `pre-malignant neoplasm`, because the concept is intended to capture a stage before neoplasm formation\n+- Modeling it as a child of `precancerous condition` is consistent with that discussion and with the existing MONDO distinction between precancerous conditions and neoplasms\n+\n+Validation performed:\n+- Read the imported issue context and comments to resolve the modeling decision\n+- Checked existing MONDO terms including `MONDO:0021074 precancerous condition` and `MONDO:0000611 pre-malignant neoplasm`\n+- Verified that the cited PMIDs exist and are contextually related to precancerous/preneoplastic lesion usage via PubMed lookups\n+- Verified the new MONDO ID slot was unused before adding `MONDO:7770012`\n+- Ran local syntax conversion with `robot convert --catalog src/ontology/catalog-v001.xml -i src/ontology/mondo-edit.obo -f obo -o src/ontology/mondo-edit.TMP.obo`\n+\n+Notes:\n+- I could not run the repo's preferred ODK normalization step (`make NORM`) because the environment does not have `docker`, and `src/ontology/run.sh` depends on Docker. The ontology edit was still syntax-checked successfully with local `robot convert`.\n+\n+Completed checklist:\n+- [x] Reviewed issue title, body, and comments\n+- [x] Confirmed parent term choice from issue discussion\n+- [x] Checked for existing competing terms in MONDO\n+- [x] Minted a new unused MONDO ID\n+- [x] Added definition and issue tracker annotation\n+- [x] Ran syntax validation available in this environment\n+- [x] Committed only the ontology file I edited\n*** End Patch"},"output":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA ISSUE_COMMENTS.md\nA PR_COMMENTS.md","metadata":{"diff":"Index: /__w/eval-ont-agent-mondo/eval-ont-agent-mondo/ISSUE_COMMENTS.md\n===================================================================\n--- /__w/eval-ont-agent-mondo/eval-ont-agent-mondo/ISSUE_COMMENTS.md\n+++ /__w/eval-ont-agent-mondo/eval-ont-agent-mondo/ISSUE_COMMENTS.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,3 @@\n+Implemented locally and committed; changes can be referenced in PR #<NN>.\n+\n+Added new term `MONDO:7770012` `preneoplastic lesion` as a child of `MONDO:0021074` `precancerous condition`, following the issue discussion that it should not be modeled as a subtype of `pre-malignant neoplasm`.\n\nIndex: /__w/eval-ont-agent-mondo/eval-ont-agent-mondo/PR_COMMENTS.md\n===================================================================\n--- /__w/eval-ont-agent-mondo/eval-ont-agent-mondo/PR_COMMENTS.md\n+++ /__w/eval-ont-agent-mondo/eval-ont-agent-mondo/PR_COMMENTS.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,31 @@\n+Added a new MONDO term for `preneoplastic lesion` and committed it locally.\n+\n+